import lib/graphics.dl
import lib/geometry.dl
import tests/games/geometry_dash/physics.dl

a point at x {integer:x} and y {integer:y} means: @intrinsic("construct", a point, @intrinsic("construct", an aggregate of 2 integer values, x, y))
a color with red {integer:red}, green {integer:green} and blue {integer:blue} means: @intrinsic("construct", a color, @intrinsic("construct", an aggregate of 3 integer values, red, green, blue))
to draw the static world in {graphics frame:frame}:
	draw a rectangle at x 0 and y 0 with width the window width and height the world height in color red 18, green 18 and blue 24 in frame
	draw a rectangle at x 0 and y 0 with width the window width and height the ceiling height in color red 92, green 58 and blue 34 in frame
	draw a rectangle at x 0 and y the ground height with width the window width and height (the world height - the ground height) in color red 40, green 28 and blue 18 in frame

to draw a runner at {a point:position} with {a color:color} in {graphics frame:frame}:
	draw a rectangle at x position's x and y position's y with width the player size and height the player size in color red color's red, green color's green and blue color's blue in frame
